    REPORT.write_text('''# Package 0090 R5N.2A4.2 — Reader effective ACL\n\nDerived from the immutable closed 390-edge contract graph, not from a desired grant list. Typed reachability distinguishes invocation, confined projection, pure data processing, authenticated self-session receipt, opaque capability use, observed authority rules and foreign custody/native principals. Ownership or PUBLIC ACL observations do not transfer authority.\n\nThe source invocations establish a finite stage fixed point; bridge facts arrive under their original self-session authority. Pure stages depend on projected immutable frames and never receive a database descriptor. All graph edges have an explicit disposition and ACL result; every predicate node has a pure-evaluation entry. The five forbidden-capability conclusions are computed after edge interpretation and transitive capability-state closure.\n\nRaw config/body processing remains a sensitive source surface, explicitly classified REDACTED inside the trusted membrane; approved assertions/digests are not raw secret retrieval. Protected stats slots remain POLICY_NOT_ACQUIRED, distinct from observed NULL and separate bridge-selected facts. Opaque use of the Reader session capability does not expose credential material. Other credential custodians/native participants are not reachable as Reader authority.\n\nPUBLIC/owner/member/default privilege constructors describe catalog rules, not automatically active Reader privileges. The accepted fixed-operation ingress and session custody prohibit arbitrary SQL/protocol/identifier submission, including implicit PUBLIC-executable breadth. No physical revocation of PostgreSQL PUBLIC defaults or installed ACL is claimed. Any implementation that exposes broader authority fails the unchanged acceptance contract.\n\nACL results distinguish ALLOW, DENY, NOT_REACHABLE, REDACTED, CONDITIONALLY_VISIBLE and FUTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_BOUNDARY. Critical UNKNOWN cannot be encoded as DENY. Static conclusions apply only under the accepted fixed contract. Physical authentication, actual role/object/default ACL audit, machine-call effects and runtime confinement remain future proof obligations.\n\nReader remains the auxiliary READ_PROXY, outside the seven native participants. No graph/G1/G2/prior evidence is changed. No application implementation, SQL, database contact, native build/runtime, V043, B02, role/grant/membership changes, credentials, staging, commit or push. Qualification Input Resolution and Substitution Static Witnesses remain OPEN_BY_DEPENDENCY and are not executed.\n\nSee gate.json, test-results.json, independent-review.json and adversarial-review.json for the measured final decision; SHA256-MANIFEST.json seals this evidence. NEXT_EXECUTED=false.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
